# The security tools XenithOS Desktop comes with (the xenithos-security-tools package), all from
# Ubuntu's own archive so they update with the system.
# Not in Ubuntu 24.04, so not here yet: Metasploit, Burp Suite, ZAP, Ghidra, radare2, wpscan, recon-ng.
#
# This list is also the Apps menu's Security Tools group (the package carries a copy, and
# /usr/lib/xenithos-desktop/desktop-entries reads it):
#   ## Name: a few words about it {icon}     starts a group inside Security Tools
#   package                                  a tool, in the group above it
#   package   Name in the menu               the same, with a name of its own in the menu
# A tool with a window keeps its own menu entry, moved into its group. One that's used by
# typing gets an entry that opens a terminal on it (/usr/lib/xenithos-desktop/tool-terminal).

